@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.
   Guarded by MailerLitePageRenderTests (step 12). *@
@using Humans.Base.Extensions
@using Humans.MailerLite
@using Humans.MailerLite.Services
@using Humans.MailerLite.Services.Dtos
@using Humans.Base
@using Humans.Base.Models.Tables
@* MailerLite carries no resource set of its own: the admin pages are English operator
   copy and there is not one Localizer[…] call in them (step 3b's "does the section have
   any keys" opens with no). MailerLiteArchitectureTests.SectionTypesTakeNoStringLocalizer is
   what makes adding copy fail the build instead of silently resolving against the ambient
   SharedResource the host used to supply through this file. *@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@* A section can only addTagHelper against Humans.UI — a Shell-resident component renders
   as inert literal markup (step 6). <vc:human>, the one the debug and import pages use, is
   in Humans.UI already. *@
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Base
